					positive. Llama-code was flat on dev, at −0.006, sitting on a 0.913 ceiling. On test it landed at
					+0.0674 [+0.0304, +0.1097]. So the dev null was ceiling noise. Second, the weakest cell that survives
					is Qwen-v1 summarization. It comes in at +0.0544, with P(Δ≤0) = 0.027 and a percentile CI lower bound
					of −0.002. That clears the p&lt;0.05 bar we set in advance. We flag it as the margin to watch in any
					re-run. One more oddity we record but do not explain: on Llama the <code>special</code> category
					accepts at 0.007 (n=883). The likely cause is a gap in how chat templates and special tokens are
					handled, not an acceptance effect. We leave it out of the contrast.
				</p>
