				<h3 class="cas-sub">Adaptive draft length, the within-round baseline</h3>
				<p>
					We replay draft-length policies on the frozen exam set. A stop rule inside the round beats the best
					fixed count by +11.2% efficiency on Qwen-v1, 95% CI [+10.3%, +12.1%]. Across the three settings the
					range is +6.7% to +11.2%. This is the number the pre-round gate is measured against above, and for
					length it wins. It is a signal from inside the round. It reads how unsure the drafter is once drafting
					has begun.
				</p>
