					against the same target output. None of them was fine-tuned, distilled or aligned toward the target.
					The same-size <strong>Qwen2.5-Coder</strong> model only <strong>ties</strong> the Qwen2.5 generalist on
					code. The <strong>Qwen2.5-Math</strong> model is <strong>worse</strong> than the same-size generalist
					even on math. The best router over this set would pick the 1.5B generalist everywhere. Acceptance is
					about matching the <em>target's own style</em>. A generalist from the same family matches a generalist
					target better than a narrow expert does. <strong>Bigger helps. Picking an off-the-shelf specialist does
